WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.778 --> 00:00:07.447
On Saturday afternoon Amy watched Megan as her friend stood in front of the mirror in Amy's

2
00:00:07.448 --> 00:00:12.944
bedroom. Megan tilted her head, studying the French braid she'd just made in her hair. Usually Amy

3
00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:18.943
would have been right next to her, using the mirror to practice her latest trick. But today

4
00:00:18.944 --> 00:00:27.944
Amy was lying on her bed, moaning whenever Megan mentioned the previous night's talent show. "Really, Amy,

5
00:00:27.945 --> 00:00:38.180
it wasn't so bad." Megan pulled out the braid and started brushing her hair. "You want to

6
00:00:38.181 --> 00:00:46.077
talk talent show disasters? You should have seen Brett Greenberg. He had his gigantic dog, Rex, onstage.

7
00:00:46.078 --> 00:00:54.989
Rex was supposed to bark on command and balance a treat on his nose. But Rex ran

8
00:00:54.990 --> 00:01:03.577
to Brett's sister in the audience. And then—" Amy groaned loudly. "You're comparing me to a dog,

9
00:01:03.578 --> 00:01:11.164
Megan. This is not consoling me!" "That's not what I meant. I know I've already apologized,

10
00:01:11.165 --> 00:01:16.393
but I'm really, really sorry for messing up your trick. I shouldn't have been talking on the

11
00:01:16.394 --> 00:01:24.735
phone, and I didn't mean to drop the cards." Amy nodded. "I know you didn't mean to

12
00:01:24.736 --> 00:01:31.964
do all that stuff, Megan, but I looked like an idiot onstage! I haven't even turned on

13
00:01:31.965 --> 00:01:37.709
my phone today. I'm too afraid to see what everyone's saying about me." "Well, you don't have

14
00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:47.441
to worry about that. Everybody's still talking about Brett's dog. Brett tried to go after Rex, but

15
00:01:47.442 --> 00:01:54.440
the dog ran up to Mrs. Antonelli. He put his paws right on her shoulders and licked

16
00:01:54.441 --> 00:01:59.280
her face and her glasses!" Amy couldn't help laughing. "Who's Mrs. Antonelli?" "She's substituting for that seventh-grade

17
00:01:59.281 --> 00:02:09.107
math teacher who just had twins." "Oh." Amy sat up. "Speaking of math—remember the reason you're here?

18
00:02:09.108 --> 00:02:21.748
It's for help with your math homework." Megan sighed and pulled her hair into a ponytail. "I

19
00:02:21.749 --> 00:02:30.088
hate math—absolutely, completely hate it. How can you stand it?" Amy smiled happily at the thought of

20
00:02:30.089 --> 00:02:40.824
math problems. Now that she was in eighth grade, math class focused on algebra. Amy loved working

21
00:02:40.825 --> 00:02:47.648
with graphs and equations. "It's like doing a puzzle," she said to Megan, "and the best thing

22
00:02:47.649 --> 00:02:57.388
is there's only one right answer. So when you get that, you're done. None of that endless

23
00:02:57.389 --> 00:03:02.983
revision stuff like in English class." "Yeah, but I can never find that one right answer." Megan

24
00:03:02.984 --> 00:03:08.725
made a frowning face in the mirror. "Even with a calculator." *** On Monday morning it didn't

25
00:03:08.726 --> 00:03:20.641
take long for Amy to realize that Megan had been right. No one was talking about

26
00:03:20.642 --> 00:03:29.460
her because they were too busy laughing about Brett's dog. A rumor was even circulating that Rex

27
00:03:29.461 --> 00:03:37.859
had jumped into Mrs. Antonelli's car and driven her home! But then Amy got to math class.

28
00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:46.940
"Hey, magician!" Frank Martin called from across the room. "How's that ordinary deck of cards?" Amy turned

29
00:03:46.941 --> 00:03:52.114
red. "Pretend you didn't hear him," Megan said. She sat behind Amy. But Frank wasn't through yet.

30
00:03:52.115 --> 00:04:01.418
"Nope, nothing unusual about that deck of cards— except it leaped right off the stage!" He laughed

31
00:04:01.419 --> 00:04:12.340
and the boys sitting near him joined in. Megan jumped up and charged over to Frank. "Listen

32
00:04:12.341 --> 00:04:24.330
to me, fathead. That wasn't her fault!" "Whoa! What's going on here?" Mr. Carlson hurried into his

33
00:04:24.331 --> 00:04:30.472
classroom. "Everybody should be in their seats." "He means you, lovely assistant," Frank said in a mocking

34
00:04:30.473 --> 00:04:36.239
voice. Megan glared at him before stomping back to her seat. "Thanks, Megan," Amy whispered. "It was

35
00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:42.642
the least I could do." Amy immediately caught on to the day's lesson, but Megan seemed hopelessly

36
00:04:42.643 --> 00:04:48.387
lost. When Mr. Carlson gave permission to start the homework in class, Megan asked Amy for help.

37
00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:52.705
"You're so smart!" she said as Amy showed her how to solve the first problem. "Why don't

38
00:04:52.706 --> 00:05:01.209
you raise your hand whenever Mr. Carlson asks a question?" Amy shrugged. "I don't like talking in

39
00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:05.960
class." "But you could have a million extra-credit points for class participation!" Amy shrugged again."I don't need

40
00:05:05.961 --> 00:05:17.282
any extra credit." The bell rang to signal the end of class. As Amy passed Mr. Carlson's

41
00:05:17.283 --> 00:05:24.035
desk, he called her over. "That was a tough crowd you had the other night. Even

42
00:05:24.036 --> 00:05:28.024
the famous magician Houdini couldn't have controlled that group." Amy nodded. She didn't know what to say.

43
00:05:28.025 --> 00:05:33.941
Mr. Carlson went on. "You may not know this, but I'm an amateur magician. You probably would

44
00:05:33.942 --> 00:05:38.701
have had better luck with a trick that people could actually see." "They saw the cards fall!"

45
00:05:38.702 --> 00:05:43.094
Amy blurted out. Mr. Carlson smiled. "They sure did, but that wasn't your fault. Look, I want

46
00:05:43.095 --> 00:05:48.918
you to be the first to know something—I'm starting a magic club at school." "Thanks, Mr. Carlson,

47
00:05:48.919 --> 00:05:55.004
but I don't want to do magic anymore. I have to go now or I'll be late

48
00:05:55.005 --> 00:06:03.481
for my next class." "Think about it!" Mr. Carlson called after Amy. *** Amy did think about

49
00:06:03.482 --> 00:06:07.159
it. She thought about how she loved magic and she wanted to learn some new tricks. But

50
00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:14.062
then she thought about how she didn't want to perform for an audience—no matter how small—ever again.

51
00:06:14.063 --> 00:06:21.825
When she mentioned her dilemma to her parents, they said it was up to her to decide.

52
00:06:21.826 --> 00:06:27.562
Amy tried to forget about the club, but she passed the sign-up sheet on Mr. Carlson's bulletin

53
00:06:27.563 --> 00:06:40.123
board every day. After a week she stood there staring at it. "Maybe I should just try

54
00:06:40.124 --> 00:06:51.047
it," she thought. But as she started to write her name, she noticed something: everyone on the

55
00:06:51.048 --> 00:07:03.355
sheet was a boy. "You didn't sign up because it's all boys?" Megan squeaked at her later,

56
00:07:03.356 --> 00:07:08.431
when Amy sat down in math class. "That sounds like the perfect club to me!" Amy shook

57
00:07:08.432 --> 00:07:18.093
her head, remembering Frank and the other boys laughing at her. "Look, I'm trying out for

58
00:07:18.094 --> 00:07:24.512
the school musical, and once rehearsals start I won't have much time to hang out with you.

59
00:07:24.513 --> 00:07:31.353
Unless, of course, you do the musical too." "No, no!" Amy shook her head vigorously. "Not a

60
00:07:31.354 --> 00:07:39.909
good idea." "Amy, why are you shaking your head?" Mr. Carlson walked over and put his hand

61
00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:47.639
near her ear. "Oh, here's the problem!" He held out a quarter. "You had some money in

62
00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:53.072
your ear." He closed his hand around the coin. When he opened his fingers again, he was

63
00:07:53.073 --> 00:08:02.051
holding five nickels. Amy laughed and Megan clapped her hands. "So, Amy, how about joining magic club?"

64
00:08:02.052 --> 00:08:08.137
Mr. Carlson asked as he made all the coins disappear. Amy put her name on the list.

